body:
Valid, fixed in bdecea5. While `WARMBLY_OIDC_FIRST_USER_OWNER` is on and the instance has no accounts, the patch now:

- refuses password sign-ups in `signupAllowed` (both `RegistrationStart` and the code-confirm re-check go through it), ahead of the `PublicSignupsAllowed` and empty-instance exemptions;
- refuses non-OIDC federated sign-ups (Apple, Google) in `resolveFederated`;
- reports `registration: "true"` (closed) from `RegistrationMode`, so the login screen shows no sign-up form.

The OIDC path (`federatedSignupAllowed`), `warmblyctl setup-link` (`bootstrap.Claim`) and `warmblyctl user create` call the repository directly and are unaffected. With the option off, or once any account exists, upstream behaviour is unchanged.

Verified: the patch applies cleanly to 63f10ef; `go build` passes for auth, handler and repository, and so does `go test ./internal/app/auth/`. A scratch table test covered reserved, claimed, off and unset cases for `signupAllowed`, `RegistrationMode` and `firstOwnerCandidate`. On the claimed test install, `/v1/auth/config` reports `invite_only`, an uninvited `POST /v1/auth/register` returns `registration_invite_only`, and OIDC begin still returns the Cloudron provider URL.
